.TH "FONTFACESET.LOADING_EVENT" "3JS" "October 27, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
FontFaceSet.loading_event \- FontFaceSet: loading event
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[CR]loading\f[R] event fires when the document begins loading
fonts.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqloading\(dq, (event) => { })
.EE
.PP
Alternatively, assign to the event handler property of the interface:
.IP
.EX
onloading = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EXAMPLE
In the following example, when the font \f[CR]Ephesis\f[R] starts to
load, \(lqFont is loading\&...\(rq is printed to the console.
.IP
.EX
document.fonts.onloading = () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(\(dqFont is loading\(dq);
};

(\f[B]async\f[R] () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]await\f[R] document.fonts.load(\(dq16px Ephesis\(dq);
})();
.EE
